2435-/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-q5kjta/TASK-260728-q5kjta_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-4843d1.log:2265:-1. Every up-front grant is performed in ONE human session and the session record states the start and end time and that no producer or reviewer cycle occurred inside it. 2. The login Keychain is unlocked and always-allow private-key access is granted for the Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities to the named unattended signing tools; the record names the identities by common name and the tools granted, never key material. 3. An authenticated Xcode/Apple Developer portal session for the Relux Works team exists and the operator has confirmed authority to create the macOS entries in the approved matrix; two-factor is completed during this sitting. 4. Creation and download of exactly the approved macOS entries is authorized and nothing beyond them: the four macOS App IDs works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel; the Network Extensions capability on those four; and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Mac registered. The record states explicitly that NO App Group record was created, that the App Groups capability was enabled on no App ID, that no Keychain access group portal mutation was performed or required, and that no Developer ID or App Store distribution profile was created. All FOUR iOS App IDs (works.relux.tunnel.ios, works.relux.tunnel.ios.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios.tunnel) are explicitly NOT authorized because iOS is deferred under ADR-024, and works.relux.proxy is not touched. 5. A NAMED notarytool credential profile is stored in the login Keychain and the owner states the disposition for the source App Store Connect API private-key file; only the profile name and the chosen disposition are recorded, never the file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes. 6. The Sparkle ed25519 keypair is generated with the pinned vendor tool and the private key is placed in approved custody; only the custody location name is recorded here. 7. Shell history and command echo are suppressed for every credential command, and a post-ceremony scan of the repository, board resources, run logs, and shell history finds no secret value, key path, key ID, issuer ID, or account credential. 8. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records which grants succeeded, which were declined, and any residual interaction the portal may still force later; a declined grant is recorded as a named blocker on the specific downstream task rather than as an assumed grant.
